# Dependencies (prettier ignores node_modules by default; listed for clarity)
node_modules/

# Lockfiles — managed by the package manager, not hand-formatted
package-lock.json

# Per-pipeline scratch dir (flow worktrees register this in .git/info/exclude)
.flow-tmp/

# These markdown files conflict with existing structural guards in
# bin/skill-md-lint.test.ts, so prettier is not allowed to manage them.
# Each is still guarded by its own lint/anchor; re-enable here only if
# the upstream cause is resolved.
#
# Non-idempotent: two consecutive `prettier --write` passes oscillate a
# deeply-nested fenced code block's indentation (16 <-> 20 spaces) with
# no fixpoint, so `prettier --check .` could never pass on it.
skills/pipeline/flow-pipeline/SKILL.md
# Reformatting grows it past the 34000-char budget skill-md-lint enforces
# (keeps AGENTS.md clear of Claude Code's 40k per-session warning).
AGENTS.md
# Prettier re-pads a markdown table whose exact header skill-md-lint
# anchors on ('| Status | Escalation tag |').
skills/pipeline/flow-pr-review/SKILL.md

# Shell-script fixtures pinning byte-exact rendered hook bodies
# (base-branch-guard.test.ts's version-drift lock byte-compares these
# against BASE_BRANCH_GUARD_HOOK / LEGACY_HOOK_BODIES). Prettier ships no
# shell parser, so `prettier --check .` errors on any *.sh file rather than
# just leaving it unformatted — ignore the extension, not just these files.
bin/fixtures/*.sh

# model-bench fixtures: prettier checks .json/.md/.ts and would reformat
# fixtures whose truth.json keys defects on file+line, silently invalidating
# the ground truth.
bin/fixtures/model-bench/

# model-bench report: report.md is generated by renderReport and then
# hand-appended with two authored sections, so a --write normalisation pass
# could never be kept idempotent.
docs/model-bench/

# flow-eval fixtures: planted-defect / real-repo content that must stay
# byte-exact for the graders (an off-by-one bug, a type error, committed
# state.json/pr.json truth) — a --write pass would silently invalidate what
# the scenario is measuring. evals/_shims/ ships a `gh` CLI shim, not
# hand-formatted TS. bin/fixtures/eval/ mirrors the bin/fixtures/model-bench/
# precedent for a captured, byte-sensitive transcript.
evals/*/*/fixture/
evals/*/*/overlay/
evals/*/*/preload/
evals/_shims/
bin/fixtures/eval/

# flow-eval baseline: report.json/summary.md are generated by
# buildReport/renderSummary, and README.md's recorded-at table is refreshed
# by the baseline writer between markers — none of these are hand-formatted.
docs/eval/baseline/
